# Lesson 3, part 4: extracting the yield to maturity when the price is known. Questions 5, 6 and 7 of the lesson 2 file.
# The file repeats the cash-flow table for each price; here section a is solved in the table (IRR), and sections b and c with RATE.
assert [round(_fin.RATE(6, 5, -P, 100), 4) for P in (100, 90, 110)] == [0.05, 0.071, 0.0315]
assert [round((1 + _fin.RATE(20, 0.75, -P, 100)) ** 4 - 1, 4) for P in (100, 90, 110)] == [0.0303, 0.054, 0.0095]
assert round((1 + _fin.IRR([-105, 3, 23, 2.4, 22.4, 1.8, 21.8, 1.2, 21.2, 0.6, 20.6])) ** 2 - 1, 4) == 0.0423
assert round((1 + _fin.RATE(8, 35, -1040, 1000)) ** 2 - 1, 4) == 0.0595

